# Architecture

- Compose functions render immutable UI state and emit user actions.
- ViewModels coordinate use cases/repositories and expose UI state.
- Repository interfaces belong in framework-free code; implementations own I/O.
- Use constructor injection and Hilt bindings for repository implementations.
- Keep Android APIs in the UI/application layer; domain contracts stay
  framework-free.
- Use Kotlin coroutines and Flow for asynchronous state and Retrofit/OkHttp for
  network boundaries.
- Features must not reach into another feature's presentation layer.
- Add an abstraction only for a real boundary or focused test seam.
